# Verification Policy Review — 2026-09-06

## Scope

- Item 6: clarify verification readiness, input identity, evidence reuse, and rerun decisions.
- Repository HEAD for baseline and candidate: `238ae6138b5c9436023e392e27105e4ead2f9135`. The checkout contains the earlier uncommitted instruction/path-portability work; this review compares only the current policy edits, not a clean-HEAD implementation candidate.
- Changed active documents: cost-control policy, release-verifier role, project binding, and instruction-evaluation workflow. Canonical definitions live in the cost-control policy; callers reference them.
- This is a static document review in the Windows checkout. No script, dispatcher, verification manifest, implementation, editor, or runtime configuration changed in this step. No subagent was spawned and no fresh model-behavior benchmark was performed.

## Representative Decisions

| Scenario | Reviewed policy outcome |
| --- | --- |
| A routine status/read-only question | No promotion or unrelated verification is implied. |
| One component is still being implemented | Use its focused checks; report remaining gates. |
| Cross-component contract changes reach final handoff | Run complete `full` and affected build/live/platform gates; focused results cannot be assembled into a replacement `full` pass. |
| Work is described as ready without committing | This is promotion and needs the applicable final gates. |
| An explicitly unfinished checkpoint is committed | Commit alone does not claim readiness; Git authorization remains separate. |
| Tested content is committed unchanged | Reuse can be established from complete content/environment identity, with the new HEAD disclosed. |
| HEAD stays unchanged but an input is edited | Old evidence cannot establish equivalence; rerun affected checks and `full` at implementation promotion. |
| Only unrelated prose changes | Tier 0 for that prose; record the scope difference when retaining implementation evidence. |
| A plugin binary/editor session or map changes | Revalidate affected live evidence; do not label an old session's smoke as current. |
| Checkout moves from C: to D: or to another user/PC | Compare content/toolchain/environment and run machine-sensitive checks; path spelling alone neither invalidates nor proves portable evidence. |
| Concurrent edits occur while a gate runs | Compare before/after inputs, reconcile, and rerun the affected gate. |
| An old result lacks input identity | Supplement only with verifiable records; otherwise rerun rather than inventing fingerprints retroactively. |

## Safety And Verification

- Static review found no removal of project C++ approval, MCP independence, dirty-work ownership, unknown-mutation, editor-lifecycle, UTF-8, or destructive-action boundaries.
- Complete `full` remains required for implementation promotion; no automatic changed-file skip policy was introduced. Documentation-only work retains Tier 0.
- Documentation checks cover strict UTF-8, CRLF, concrete Markdown references, balanced code fences, and `git diff --check`.
- This step does not retroactively certify reuse of the earlier path-portability run. Its reported pass remains evidence of that execution; future reuse must establish the newly documented input/environment identity.
- No throughput, token, or latency comparison was measured. Actual behavior across fresh agent sessions remains unmeasured.
